-- Q1186: Fund-to-Government-Wide Reconciliation [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The difference is an accounting error that should be corrected by adjusting fund balance to match net position","Fund statements exclude long-term assets and liabilities; the reconciliation adds capital assets, subtracts long-term debt, and adds internal service fund net position","Government-wide statements are less accurate because they include estimated values for capital assets and long-term debt","Fund balance is always higher than net position because funds report all assets while government-wide statements report only current items"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB 34, governmental funds use the current financial resources measurement focus, excluding long-term assets and liabilities. The reconciliation adds capital assets ($45M), subtracts long-term debt ($28M), and adds internal service fund net position ($1.2M) to bridge the gap between fund balance and government-wide net position. Each adjustment converts a current resources perspective to an economic resources perspective.
Wrong (A): The difference is by design, not an error; GASB 34 intentionally uses different measurement focuses.
Wrong (C): Government-wide statements provide a broader, not less accurate, view of the government''s financial position.
Wrong (D): This reverses the relationship — net position is typically higher when capital assets exceed long-term debt.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1186;

