-- Q1190: Fund-to-Government-Wide Reconciliation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The $450,000 is recognized as revenue on both statements because the taxes have been levied and are legally collectible","The $450,000 is excluded from both statements because uncollected taxes are not reported until cash is received","On fund statements the $450,000 is a deferred inflow because it fails the 60-day availability test; on government-wide it is revenue","The deferred inflow appears on government-wide statements while fund statements recognize the full revenue more aggressively"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under modified accrual accounting, revenue must be both measurable and available. The $450,000 expected within 90 days exceeds the city''s 60-day availability period, so it is reported as a deferred inflow on fund statements. On government-wide statements (full accrual), revenue is recognized at levy when the enforceable legal claim arises, so the full $450,000 is revenue. The reconciliation adds $450,000 to revenue.
Wrong (A): The availability criterion on fund statements prevents recognition of amounts collectible beyond the 60-day window.
Wrong (B): Modified accrual recognizes the receivable; it is the revenue recognition that is deferred, not the asset.
